    "basis": "Buffet attendant/clearer at ~1 per 40 guests for the lighter, staggered breakfast/lunch (early shift) and ~1 per 30 guests at dinner (late shift), rounded up, minimum 1 when guests are in. Industry buffet ratios are 1 server per 20-30 guests (1:40 lean) and 1 busser per ~25 guests with china; self-serve tea/coffee is replenished by the same staff. Dedicated plate-wash at ~1 per 80 covers per service once above ~35 guests (below that the kitchen KA/KP washes up). At 61-100 one late staffer is the designated lead; at 101-130 add a dedicated supervisor (a 'captain' for 100+ buffets).",
    "notes": "The 1:40 early-shift ratio and the 20-30 minute overlap timing are judgement calls, not published figures.",
    "sources": [
      "https://www.quickstaffpro.com/event-staff-scheduling/event-staffing-ratios-catering-success",
      "https://www.quickstaffpro.com/event-staff-scheduling/catering-staff-roles-full-service-vs-buffet-events",
      "https://univents.app/en/free-tools/staffing-calculator",
      "https://feedtheline.org/uncategorized/catering-staff-to-guest-ratio-large-buffet",
      "https://www.hospitalitycalculators.com/tool/catering/event-staffing"
    ]
  },
