    "basis": "Rule: one named person in charge whenever guests are on site. Below 36 guests the GM or a head of department covers the early slot. Overnight, UK fire safety guidance for sleeping accommodation requires enough trained staff for night-time evacuation, so there is always 1 sleep-in responder when guests are present (using the 42nd room). Above ~100 guests, consider 2 night responders per the fire risk assessment. Shifts follow UK rest-break rules (20 min break for more than 6h worked).",
